# Code style

When writing Java (only after the user **explicitly** asks to implement):

- Reuse first. One pagination binder, one 404 access check, one time parse/format, one Reminder `INSERT … SELECT` for create and reschedule, one `NotificationSender`, one error body.
- No copy-paste. No second clock in Java. No full-graph load for mail.
- Smallest diff. Refactor only what you touch. Delete new dead code.
- Shared cross-cutting in `com.dealership.shared`. Native SQL stays with the owning module.
- Passwords BCrypt. Email lowercase unique. VIN uppercase unique. Details: `docs/trd/code-style.md`.
